 # Her Flight Deck — current project status
 
-M2 PR1 source review completed on 5 October 2026: R1–R4 and remaining startup/FK/rollback corrections verified; 2,498 frontend and 386 Rust tests pass. Integration is conditional on required CI before merge. See [completion review](docs/M2_PRACTICE_SESSION_PR1_COMPLETION_REVIEW_2026-10-05.md) and [PR2 assignment](docs/M2_PRACTICE_SESSION_PR2_PROMPT_2026-10-05.md). Installed/release gates remain separate.
+**5 October 2026: M2 practice-session PR2 finish corrections implemented, pending Codex independent review.** The eight failing behaviors and the invalid gate claim from the [PR2 correction rereview](docs/M2_PRACTICE_SESSION_PR2_REREVIEW_2026-10-05.md) are closed on top of accepted PR1 and the passing PR2 corrections. The panel now owns one reducer phase machine gated by request generation with a synchronous intent lock (M2UI-R5, M2UI-R6), keeps pending/error/retry presentation reachable from the completed result and reconciles a retake against the real current attempt (M2UI-R7), and reconciles null/closed/replaced state through one adoption path (M2UI-R8). History views use per-route generations that survive an A→B→A round trip, a synchronous per-key erasure lock, one bounded pending confirmation dialog, and attempt revalidation when only the history key changes (M2UI-R9). The rereview's frozen diagnostic passed verbatim (92/92, exit 0) before being removed; its eight behaviors plus 15 extensions are permanent in `src/pages/StudyLibrary/PracticeSessionPR2Finish.test.ts`, and the ten earlier promoted positives are untouched. Exits are now captured per step with no `tee` masking: the final sequential gate is 9/9 exit 0 — typecheck, `npm test` 2,545 passed / 4 skipped / **zero unhandled errors**, build, 391 Rust passed / 6 ignored, Clippy `-D warnings`, fmt, cargo-lock, whitespace/final-newline hygiene, and migrations 1–11 plus the checksum registry unchanged. The two previously missing proofs were added: native erasure mid-write rollback and browser erasure disabled-recovery. The earlier run's two unhandled `DatabaseDisabledError` rejections did not recur in one full plus three isolated runs of the implicated file; nothing was suppressed and no production recovery semantics were changed, and the failed receipt is preserved. Gating this work caught and fixed two further defects in it: a load-dependent focus race (feedback reveal disables the focused choice, so the focus hand-off now runs in a layout effect) and a conflict message that announced a refresh before the authoritative read succeeded. All changes stay uncommitted and unpushed in `/Users/rickymac/code/Flight-training-pr70-integration` on branch `codex/m2-practice-session-ui`. Stopped before Git integration, new roadmap features, app launch against user data, signing, packaging or release. See [finish-corrections report](docs/evidence/m2-practice-session-pr2-finish-corrections-2026-10-05/submitted-report.md) and [evidence manifest](docs/evidence/m2-practice-session-pr2-finish-corrections-2026-10-05/README.md).
+
+**5 October 2026 (earlier round, now superseded):** PR2 corrections for M2UI-R1–R4 were submitted as "all 8 sequential integration gates passed". The independent rereview above confirms the ten promoted diagnostics pass but **invalidates that gate claim**: its own attached `npm test` receipt records two unhandled `DatabaseDisabledError` rejections despite the reported exit 0, and its closure map names three permanent cases that `src/pages/StudyLibrary/PracticeSessionPR2Corrections.test.ts` does not contain. That submission's report and receipts are preserved unchanged at [docs/evidence/m2-practice-session-pr2-corrections-2026-10-05](docs/evidence/m2-practice-session-pr2-corrections-2026-10-05/README.md); its ten diagnostics remain the accepted passing baseline, and its remaining gaps are the R5–R10 work closed in the entry above.
+
+M2 PR1 source review completed on 5 October 2026: R1–R4 and remaining startup/FK/rollback corrections verified; 2,498 frontend and 386 Rust tests pass. Integration merged through PR #101, commit 61031d4c7143fdf181bba2cc18616c5345521c3e. See [completion review](docs/M2_PRACTICE_SESSION_PR1_COMPLETION_REVIEW_2026-10-05.md) and [PR2 assignment](docs/M2_PRACTICE_SESSION_PR2_PROMPT_2026-10-05.md). Installed/release gates remain separate.
 
 **4 October M2 PR 1 initialization re-review — R3 still open:** [Review](docs/M2_PRACTICE_SESSION_PR1_READINESS_REVIEW_2026-10-04.md) verifies all previous boundary fixes, 29 frontend passes and171 existing native passes. Three additional failures remain: browser invalid-state reopen, missing schema FK definition and conversion committed before semantic failure. [One focused model-neutral assignment](docs/M2_PRACTICE_SESSION_PR1_READINESS_CORRECTIONS_PROMPT_2026-10-04.md) completes actual browser validation, FK metadata and atomic initialization while preserving closed fixes. Source stays uncommitted/unaccepted; PR2 and installed/signing/release work deferred.
 
